  clock: 4  # 7498
  nonce: '7498'  # 7498
  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nRE-CHECKED AT TIP: THE GATE STILL DOES NOT EXIST, so this item is accurate and unstarted. Searched scripts/ and the test tree at dev 11a240f83d for a test-only-reachability check; nothing implements it (dead-code-prospector-run.py and measure-catalogue-reach.py are different questions -- prospecting and catalogue coverage, not 'production symbol reachable only from its own test module').\n\nThe class this item was filed for is unchanged and its members are still live: the section 3a arm consumes nothing in production (INV-lupav, INV-sadah), and WI-joluk's gate is wired to one of two arms by design. So the family this item generalises is not hypothetical, and the recurrence-prevention it proposes still has nothing standing in for it."  # 7498
- op: discuss  # ac13
  at: '2026-08-21T19:25:31Z'  # ac13
  by: agent  # ac13
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ac13
  clock: 5  # ac13
  nonce: ac13  # ac13
  message: "THE RE-SCOPED QUESTION IS MEASURED, AND BOTH 2026-08-05 DISQUALIFIERS FALL.\n2026-08-21, dev 09921c57a1, on a full self-survey (5,251 production callable\nsymbols, 206MB behaviour map).\n\nThe owner ruling refused the gate AS FILED and re-scoped it to the question in\nthis item's own title -- \"does every DIRECT CALLER of this symbol live in a test\nmodule\" -- rather than dead-code-maybe's \"is this reachable from the production\nseed set\". Nobody had measured the re-scoped question. Measured now:\n\n    production callable symbols               5,251\n      has >=1 NON-TEST direct caller          4,248\n      ZERO direct callers                       414\n      ALL direct callers are test modules       589   <== THE COHORT\n\nDISQUALIFIER 1 -- COHORT SIZE. Was 1,747 and \"would fail CI ~1747 times on day\none\". Re-scoped: 589. Still too many for a hard fail on day one, but this is a\nrepo that already runs a shrink-only ratchet over a 672-error surface; 589 is a\ntractable baseline, 1,747 was not.\n\nDISQUALIFIER 2 -- IT MISSED ITS OWN MOTIVATING EXAMPLES. Was 3 of 6, and the\nruling called that \"not a gate\". Re-scoped, run against the ADR-0017 family by\nname:\n\n    infer_summary              FLAGGED     (was MISSED -- is_exported seeding)\n    is_field_tainted           FLAGGED     (was MISSED)\n    select_ddg_targets         FLAGGED     (was MISSED)\n    match_source               FLAGGED\n    match_sink                 FLAGGED\n    match_sanitizer            FLAGGED\n    load_function_summaries    correctly NOT flagged\n\nSix of seven, and THE SEVENTH IS THE CONTROL: load_function_summaries is the one\nmember genuinely fixed during the campaign (PR #197 gave it two production call\nsites), and the gate does not fire on it. So the signal discriminates rather than\nflagging the family wholesale. That is what the 2026-08-05 note predicted when it\nsaid the caller-based question \"is immune to the is_exported seeding, because it\nasks about callers rather than about seeds\".\n\n*** DISQUALIFIER 3 -- THE PREREQUISITE -- DOES NOT BIND, AND THIS IS THE FINDING\nTHAT CHANGES THE PLAN. *** The ruling's honest price was: \"hypergumbo does not\nmodel its own plugin registry as reachability. Until it does, ANY test-only-\nreachability signal on this repository is dominated by dispatch.\" That was\nmeasured true for the SEED-based question -- 598 Class.method + 1,147 private\nhelpers against 2 public bare functions, i.e. 96.6% dispatch. Under the\ncaller-based question:\n\n    RE-SCOPED COHORT (589)              ZERO-CALLER COHORT (414)\n      public bare function  298  50.6%    Class.method          228  55.1%\n      Class.method          202  34.3%    private module fn     157  37.9%\n      private module fn      89  15.1%    public bare function   29   7.0%\n\nDispatch is 49.4% of the cohort, not 96.6%, and the PUBLIC BARE FUNCTION -- the\nexact shape the ADR-0017 family has, and the shape the seed-based question found\ntwo of -- is now the LARGEST bucket at 298.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, because the number is more useful with it: a registry-dispatched\nanalyzer method has NO direct callers at all (the dispatch is dynamic), so it\nlands in the ZERO-CALLER cohort, which is where dispatch actually lives (55%\nClass.method there). The caller-based question separates dispatch BY ITSELF. The\nruling assumed a demotion arm would be needed to survive dispatch; the\nmeasurement says the re-scoped question does that separation structurally, and\nthe demotion arm is not the blocker it was priced as. Modelling the plugin\nregistry remains a real and worthwhile feature -- it is just not a PREREQUISITE\nfor this gate.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT CLAIMING, stated plainly.\n  * The 589 are NOT adjudicated. I have not read a sample to see how many are\n    genuine dead production code versus legitimately test-only-called helpers.\n    A gate wants that sample before a baseline is frozen, or the baseline\n    ratifies whatever is there -- the rubber-stamp failure the ruling warns of.\n  * MY CLASSIFIERS ARE HAND-ROLLED, which this project's own rule 5 says not to\n    trust: the test-path predicate and the call-edge-type set in the measurement\n    script are mine, not production's. `taxonomy` / `test_masking` own the first\n    and `edge_types` owns the second. The shape split is unlikely to move much,\n    but the exact counts should be re-derived through production's classifiers\n    before anyone freezes a number. Script:\n    ~/... /scratchpad/ratuv_measure.py (session artifact, not committed).\n  * Shape is inferred from kind + name (dotted or method-kind => Class.method,\n    leading underscore => private), not from a containment walk.\n\nRECOMMENDED SHAPE, given the above: a SHRINK-ONLY ratchet over the caller-based\ncohort with a frozen baseline, not a hard fail -- the same instrument the mypy\nsurface uses and the same one the ruling implicitly asked for when it objected to\nday-one volume. The ruling's own words still govern the risk: \"A rubber-stamped\nratchet is worse than none.\" That argues for adjudicating a sample of the 589\nFIRST, so the baseline is a known quantity rather than a snapshot.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: todo_hard. The ruling that stopped this said DO NOT BUILD THE\nGATE AS FILED and named a prerequisite; the prerequisite is now measured not to\nbind, and the re-scoped question is measured to work. That is a change in the\ninputs to the owner's decision, not a licence to build."  # ac13
- op: discuss  # d5a4
  at: '2026-08-30T10:12:09Z'  # d5a4
  by: agent  # d5a4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d5a4
  clock: 6  # d5a4
  nonce: d5a4  # d5a4
  message: "THE TWO PRECONDITIONS THIS ITEM NAMED ARE NOW DONE. NOTHING WAS BUILT -- the\n2026-08-05 ruling (\"DO NOT BUILD THE GATE AS FILED\") is untouched, and the\n2026-08-21 note's own closing line (\"a change in the inputs to the owner's\ndecision, not a licence to build\") still governs. This is inputs.\n\nMeasured 2026-08-30 against the self-survey behaviour map at\n~/.cache/hypergumbo/f36c63310c791188/.../survey.json (46,849 nodes, 163,842\nedges, written 05:03 today, so it predates today's two merges -- disclosed\nrather than described as \"at tip\"). Rig:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/ratuv_rederive_08302026/.\n\n*** PRECONDITION 1: RE-DERIVE THROUGH PRODUCTION'S CLASSIFIERS. ***\nThe 2026-08-21 note disclaimed its own numbers -- \"MY CLASSIFIERS ARE\nHAND-ROLLED ... the exact counts should be re-derived through production's\nclassifiers before anyone freezes a number.\" Done, using\n`axis_meta_keys.call_family_edge_types()` (= {calls, instantiates}) for the edge\nset and BOTH production test predicates, because there are two and their own\ndocstrings say they \"answer different questions\" and \"diverge in both\ndirections\":\n\n                                    BROAD              NARROW\n                                    paths.is_test_file  supply_chain.is_test_file\n    production callable symbols     4,930              4,958\n      has a non-test caller         3,496              3,527\n      zero callers                    652                653\n      ALL callers are test            782                778   <== THE COHORT\n\nTHE USEFUL PART IS THAT THE TWO AGREE TO WITHIN FOUR. The cohort is robust to\nwhich production predicate you pick, so that choice cannot be used to argue the\nnumber up or down. Against the hand-rolled 589 it is ~32% larger -- but that\ndelta CONFLATES the classifier change with nine days of tree drift, and I cannot\nseparate them because the 2026-08-21 script was a session artifact and was not\ncommitted. Do not quote \"589 -> 782\" as a classifier effect.\n\nINSTRUMENT NOTE, since it nearly published a false zero: the narrow flag is\nNESTED under `supply_chain` (WI-lalip relocated it). Reading it at the node top\nlevel returns False for all 46,849 nodes and yields a clean, plausible cohort of\nZERO. Caught by a positive control asking how many nodes carry the flag at all\n(34,470 do).\n\n*** PRECONDITION 2: ADJUDICATE A SAMPLE BEFORE ANY BASELINE IS FROZEN. ***\nSeeded sample, n=30, seed=20260830, from the 782. Two results, and the first\nCONTRADICTS this thread's most recent claim.\n\n(a) DISPATCH IS IN THE COHORT, NOT SEPARATED FROM IT. The 2026-08-21 note argued\n    the caller-based question \"does that separation structurally\" because a\n    registry-dispatched method \"has NO direct callers at all, so it lands in the\n    ZERO-CALLER cohort\". That is false for any dispatched symbol whose own unit\n    test calls it directly -- which is most of them. Textual's on_*/action_*\n    handlers and @register_linker functions have test callers and no production\n    callers, so they land squarely in the 782.\n\n(b) BUT THE DEMOTION ARM IS CHEAP, AND THAT IS THE FINDING THAT MATTERS. The\n    2026-08-05 ruling priced modelling the plugin registry as the PREREQUISITE.\n    Every dispatch family in the sample is identifiable from SOURCE TEXT with no\n    dynamic modelling at all. Classified over the whole 782:\n\n      @register_linker(...) above the def          41   5.2%   dispatch\n      Textual on_*/action_* in a textual module     35   4.5%   dispatch\n      analyze_<lang> module wrapper, where the\n        module also defines `_analyzer = XAnalyzer()`\n        so the CLASS is the production path        101  12.9%   *** DEAD ***\n      unclassified                                 605  77.4%\n\n*** THE 101 ARE THE ITEM'S OWN FAMILY, AT SCALE. *** analyze_scheme,\nanalyze_apex, analyze_bibtex, analyze_gitignore and 97 peers are public bare\nfunctions whose only callers are tests, sitting beside a registered class that\nis the real production path. That is precisely the ADR-0017 shape this item was\nfiled on -- and it occurs 101 times, not six. Spot-checked: analyze_scheme has\nZERO production references anywhere under packages/*/src; scheme.py line 291\ndefines SchemeAnalyzer, line 365 does `_analyzer = SchemeAnalyzer()`, and line\n374's analyze_scheme is a shim nothing in production names.\n\n*** WHAT I AM NOT CLAIMING. ***\n  * 605 of 782 are UNCLASSIFIED and unadjudicated. The ruling's \"a rubber-stamped\n    ratchet is worse than none\" still binds: no baseline should be frozen over a\n    population that is 77% unexamined.\n  * A SHAPE WORTH A RULING SITS IN THE UNCLASSIFIED HEAD: gate implementations\n    (audit_findings.find_readme_index_drift, parse_audit_findings,\n    validate_against_registry, catalog.validate_pass_dependencies ...) are\n    production code whose only caller IS the root gate test, BY DESIGN. Flagging\n    those is noise, and no static signal separates them from a dead wrapper --\n    \"called only by tests\" is their correct steady state. Whether they are in\n    scope is a decision, not a measurement.\n  * MY OWN DISCRIMINATOR IS WEAK PER-SYMBOL and is reported only as bucket\n    counts. It counts short-name references, so `Pattern.matches` scores 497 off\n    regex `.matches` and `PhaseDuration.group` scores 669 off `.group()`. Worse\n    in the other direction: `infer_summary` scored ONE production reference, and\n    that reference is a COMMENT in taint.py:2985 reading \"(`infer_summary`) still\n    has zero production callers\". The grep counted prose about deadness as\n    evidence of life.\n\n*** RECOMMENDED NEXT INPUT, still not a build. *** Adjudicate the 605 by shape\nrather than one by one -- the sample says they cluster (per-language wrappers,\ngate implementations, availability probes, file-discovery helpers). If the\n101-member analyze_* family alone were retired or wired, that is a concrete\ndeliverable with no gate and no baseline, and it would shrink the cohort by 13%\nbefore anyone has to decide what the gate should do."  # d5a4
